  "id": "COMPOUND:29927 - PROTEIN:5849",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a consistent relationship between (4-(Prop-1-en-2-yl)cyclohexyl)methanol and A549, a human lung cancer cell line. This compound is identified as a target of multiple entities, including SNU-387 and Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, which in turn target A549. The mechanism appears to involve the compound interacting with SNU-387, which is a potential target of several compounds, including the (E)-4-hydroxy-2-methylbut-2-enoate, which also targets A549. The evidence suggests that (4-(Prop-1-en-2-yl)cyclohexyl)methanol may act as a modulator or inhibitor of SNU-387, which then exerts its effect on A549. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for this compound in targeting A549 through a complex network of interactions involving SNU-387 and other related molecules.",
